      "content": "that makes sense. so it's really about whether the pattern is something \"anyone\" in the industry would eventually learn, or if it's something uniquely theirs.\n\ni'm just a bit paranoid about the \"unaided memory\" wording though. it sounds almost... sneaky? like, it's assuming i might be hoarding these little bits of logic in the back of my mind without even realizing it. \n\nit feels like there's this tiny, hidden risk lurking in the corners of the contract where they could just claim i'm \"stashing\" their secrets. do you think there's any way the clause is actually intended to be a trap, or is it just standard stuff to cover their bases in case someone gets a bit too \"creative\" with their knowledge?",
